BT /F1 12 Tf 50 720 Td 18 TL
(Clinical Practice Guidelines: Acute Myocardial Infarction Management) '
(Section 1.1: STEMI Emergency Revascularization Window) '
(For patients presenting with ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction STEMI) '
(primary percutaneous coronary intervention PCI is the preferred strategy) '
(when performed within 90 minutes of first medical contact FMC time.) '
(If transfer to a PCI center exceeds 120 minutes intravenous fibrinolysis) '
(must be initiated within 10 minutes of diagnosis.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj << /Length 420 >> stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 720 Td 18 TL
(Section 2.3: Antiplatelet Pharmacotherapy & Absolute Contraindications) '
(All acute coronary syndrome patients should receive chewable Aspirin 162-325 mg) '
(along with Ticagrelor 180 mg loading dose or Prasugrel 60 mg loading dose.) '
(Absolute contraindications to fibrinolytic therapy include:) '
(1. Any prior history of intracranial hemorrhage ICH.) '
(2. Known structural cerebral vascular lesion.) '
(3. Active internal bleeding excluding menses.) '
(4. Ischemic stroke within preceding 3 months.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
